          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flag"} flag
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            or a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+space"} projective space
            is a nested system of linear/projective subspaces, one of each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-1
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-vector" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+variety"} projective variety
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "." do
              %strong flag variety
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is the field of real or complex numbers, then it has a structure of a smooth
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homogeneous+space"} homogeneous space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL(n,k)/B
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is the subgroup of lower (or upper if you like) triangular matrices. By the
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gram%E2%80%93Schmidt_process"} Gram–Schmidt orthogonalization procedure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi B
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL(n,\mathbb{C})/B\cong SU(n)/T
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is the subgroup of the diagonal
            = succeed "-matrices." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\times n
          %p
            More generally, the
            %strong generalized flag variety
            is the complex projective variety obtained as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi T
                  %mo ≅
                  %msup
                    %mi G
                    %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/T\cong G^{\mathbb{C}}/B
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+torus"} maximal torus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi G
                    %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G^{\mathbb{C}}
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complexification"} complexification
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi G
                    %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\subset G^{\mathbb{C}}
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borel+subgroup"} Borel subgroup
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+manifold"} Kähler manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parabolic+subgroup"} parabolics
            which includes, for example,
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmannians"} Grassmannians
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrable+systems"} integrable systems
